Subject: Skip undefined compiled variables when dumping a frame
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

A function's symbol table holds IS_INDIRECT slots for its compiled
variables, and those that are unset or not yet assigned are IS_UNDEF.
meminfo_zval_dump() passed that type to zend_get_type_by_const(), which
has no case for it and reaches ZEND_UNREACHABLE(): undefined behaviour in
a release build, and a stop under Fil-C, so meminfo_dump() died in any
frame with such a variable.

--- a/meminfo.c
+++ b/meminfo.c
@@ -311,6 +311,11 @@
         zv = Z_INDIRECT_P(zv);
     }
 
+    /* A compiled variable that was never assigned or was unset. */
+    if (Z_TYPE_P(zv) == IS_UNDEF) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     if (Z_ISREF_P(zv)) {
         ZVAL_DEREF(zv);
     }
